Portions adapted from SAP's node-rfc
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

The TypeScript layer in src/ts/ and the test suite in test/ are adapted from:

    https://github.com/SAP-archive/node-rfc
    src/ts/*.ts and test/**
    Copyright (c) 2014 SAP SE, Srdjan Boskovic <srdjan.boskovic@sap.com>
    Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0

A copy of the Apache License, Version 2.0 is available at:

    http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0

The adapted code is the binding's public API -- the classes, the type
definitions, the promise and callback duality, and the error shapes -- together
with the suite that tests them. It carries no knowledge of the RFC wire
protocol. erpl-proto's implementation of that protocol is clean-room, derived
solely from this project's own captures of libsapnwrfc, and nothing in the
adapted code informs it.

Two files depart from the reference and say so in their own comments:
src/ts/noderfc-bindings.ts, which loads a napi-rs addon rather than an SDK, and
test/utils/abapSystem.ts, which reads the system from the environment rather
than from an sapnwrfc.ini nobody outside SAP has.

